# Vetted upstream ingestion pin.
#
# This fork tracks the upstream template repo named below, and that relationship
# is PULL-ONLY: firstmate fetches from it and never pushes, opens a pull request,
# or creates any other artifact there.
#
# Two different facts, deliberately kept under two names:
#
#   sha          how far upstream has been reviewed. An UPSTREAM commit, and the
#                only value the drift count and the CI gate are computed from.
#                Upstream work counts as reviewed exactly when it is reachable
#                from here, so everything upstream published after it is
#                UNREVIEWED.
#   review_head  which state of THIS fork the review ended at. Optional, an audit
#                record only, never used to decide anything.
#
# Keeping them apart matters: a fork commit and an upstream commit answer
# different questions, and one value cannot honestly serve as both. The current
# pair records the clean review the captain re-baselined to on 2026-08-06:
# `review_head` is the fork commit that review ended at, and `sha` is
# `git merge-base <review_head> <upstream branch>`, the furthest upstream commit
# that review actually reached.
#
# Ingesting unreviewed upstream work is what this pin exists to prevent:
# upstream has previously landed code that injected the maintainer's own secrets
# into every agent launch, so ingestion is treated as adversarial by default.
#
# Advancing `sha` claims that everything newly reachable from it was reviewed.
# Make that claim only after the review, never to get a merge through.
#
# Two consumers read this file, and both are deterministic rather than advisory:
#   - bin/fm-upstream-gate.sh refuses any push or pull request to the default
#     branch that ingests upstream commits this pin does not already cover.
#   - bin/fm-bootstrap.sh reports the unreviewed-commit count at session start.
#
# Format: `key=value` lines, `#` comments, blank lines ignored. Keys are `url`,
# `branch`, `sha`, and optional `review_head`; bin/fm-upstream-pin.sh owns
# parsing and validation and refuses a file that is missing a required key or
# holds a malformed value.

url=https://github.com/kunchenguid/firstmate.git
branch=main
sha=673b6ad39d01183a19c5bd8a52675a2ee8ea06e6
review_head=f157a6b605ba3c3d85d5d4e12fad28720b453d3f
